## COMMUNICATION
An unprecedented solid-state superionic conductor was obtained by incorporating ionic liquid (IL) into mesoporous metal-organic framework (MOF). Because ILs occupying the core of mesopores behave as bulk, the hybrid shows the highest room-temperature conductivity $(4.4\times10^{-3}\mathsf{S}\mathsf{c m}^{-1}.$ ) among the IL-incorporated MOF hybrids reported to date.
